details.image_prompt:
[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two plates, each holding an open-faced whole wheat English muffin topped with a generous, fluffy portion of spinach-infused scrambled eggs. The eggs are studded with wilted, bright green baby spinach, topped with slices of ruby-red fresh tomato and patches of melted, slightly golden-brown mozzarella cheese. The 3/4 overhead angle shows the full composition, with the egg mixture piled neatly onto the toasted, golden-brown muffin halves. Beside each muffin on the matte ceramic plate is a portion of halved, vibrant red fresh strawberries. The second plate is slightly blurred in the background, creating a natural depth of field. Soft, natural side light from a window to the left highlights the glistening, molten texture of the cheese and the tender, airy structure of the scrambled eggs. The plates rest on a rustic, aged oak wood surface with visible wood grain and faint scratch marks. A rumpled linen napkin lies casually beneath one plate, and a few scattered strawberry seeds and a tiny stray leaf of spinach sit on the wooden table. There is a small, realistic sauce drip on the rim of the foreground plate. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating — lived-in, warm, authentic. Not a sterile studio setup. Slight natural imperfections: an asymmetric garnish placement, slightly uneven browning on the muffins. Include subtle traces of the cooking process: a few crumbs on the surface. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature — cozy and inviting, not cold or clinical. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image should be indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
]
